WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:01.640
Hey there, thrill-seekers!

00:00:01.640 --> 00:00:03.280
Are you ready to get crazy?

00:00:03.280 --> 00:00:05.330
Are you ready to get extreme?

00:00:05.330 --> 00:00:07.950
Are you ready to taste the real hardcore?

00:00:07.950 --> 00:00:11.840
We here at SCP Explained know that you love
a little excitement in your life.

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:16.090
You’re the kind of stone-cold, solid gold
bad dude whose idea of a relaxing afternoon

00:00:16.090 --> 00:00:21.179
is a staring contest with SCP-173 - and you’re
so tough, you’re gonna make that Peanut

00:00:21.179 --> 00:00:22.199
blink first!

00:00:22.199 --> 00:00:27.369
You’re the kind of person who’d punch
SCP-682, and make him apologize for grazing

00:00:27.369 --> 00:00:28.660
your fist.

00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:32.189
You wouldn’t even back down from the Scarlet
King himself, making this Monarch of Ultimate

00:00:32.189 --> 00:00:35.079
Despair say, “That’s pretty cool, man.

00:00:35.079 --> 00:00:36.079
Respect.”

00:00:36.079 --> 00:00:39.769
But if you want a genuine thrill ride, something
that’ll really put hair on your chest, you

00:00:39.769 --> 00:00:43.100
need to get your butt on a truly hardcore
rollercoaster.

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:44.420
What, too chicken?

00:00:44.420 --> 00:00:47.730
Afraid of a little motion sickness or something?

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:51.550
Or maybe you’ve been freaked out by some
of the so-called “horrifying accidents”

00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:56.010
that happened on rollercoasters - like the
1972 Big Dipper Disaster,

00:00:56.010 --> 00:00:59.679
or the 1986 Fantasyland Mindbender Catastrophe?

00:00:59.679 --> 00:01:00.679
Get real.

00:01:00.679 --> 00:01:04.180
When has a little death scared anyone at the
SCP Foundation?

00:01:04.180 --> 00:01:10.500
And besides, nothing is more awesome than
an extreme rollercoaster, and believe us,

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:14.830
any other rollercoaster will feel like kiddie
stuff compared to the absolute beast we’re

00:01:14.830 --> 00:01:16.750
gonna tell you about today.

00:01:16.750 --> 00:01:20.790
If you’re a rollercoaster novice, maybe
you should try something like the Takabisha,

00:01:20.790 --> 00:01:23.780
over in the Fuji-Q Highland theme park in
Japan.

00:01:23.780 --> 00:01:29.750
This baby boasts a 121-degree drop, famous
for making people fall out of their seats.

00:01:29.750 --> 00:01:33.450
Or maybe you want to try something like Yukon
Striker over in Canada.

00:01:33.450 --> 00:01:39.040
This widowmaker of a coaster has floorless
seats, a 360-degree flip, four inversions,

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:40.550
and a 75-meter drop.

00:01:40.550 --> 00:01:44.210
That’s a little too tame for your taste?

00:01:44.210 --> 00:01:48.600
If you’re feeling really brave, you can
hop on the Kingda Ka, over in the New Jersey

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:50.030
Six Flags theme park.

00:01:50.030 --> 00:01:56.420
You’ll get a super-fast ninety-degree climb,
followed by a bone-stripping 139-meter drop,

00:01:56.420 --> 00:02:01.280
a 129-foot camel hump, and a 270-degree spiral.

00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:04.820
That’ll give you a healthy dose of Vitamin
G-Force!

00:02:04.820 --> 00:02:06.700
Why are we telling you about all this?

00:02:06.700 --> 00:02:12.890
Because compared to SCP-2183, all those coasters
are like riding a tricycle with stabilizers

00:02:12.890 --> 00:02:15.160
in your mom’s backyard.

00:02:15.160 --> 00:02:21.570
There is no coaster more powerful, more thrilling,
and more adrenaline-pumping than SCP-2183.

00:02:21.570 --> 00:02:24.890
Let’s take a look at some of the specs.

00:02:24.890 --> 00:02:28.870
You can find this bad boy in an undisclosed
location somewhere in Idaho.

00:02:28.870 --> 00:02:33.230
This ride is so hardcore, the killjoys over
at the SCP Foundation don’t want you to

00:02:33.230 --> 00:02:34.230
ride it.

00:02:34.230 --> 00:02:38.420
But if the lame-o’s over at the Foundation
had their way, nobody would be having any

00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:39.420
fun!

00:02:39.420 --> 00:02:45.880
Look at how they put the kibosh on the Carnival
of Horrors, or as they call it, “SCP-823.”

00:02:45.880 --> 00:02:50.010
Anyone who wants to go on one of those rides
will just meet the business end of a Foundation

00:02:50.010 --> 00:02:51.480
sniper rifle.

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:54.840
And think about all the kids who’ve been
deprived of the awesome childhood experience

00:02:54.840 --> 00:03:01.510
of Cragglewood Park, aka SCP-2571, because
the Foundation party poopers decided to rain

00:03:01.510 --> 00:03:03.230
on everybody’s parade.

00:03:03.230 --> 00:03:07.070
It’s safe to say that if the Foundation
wants to keep you away from it, you’re gonna

00:03:07.070 --> 00:03:13.270
have a dope time with it, and the SCP-2183
rollercoaster is no exception.

00:03:13.270 --> 00:03:18.590
They have the whole park blocked off and patrolled
by at least four security guards at any given

00:03:18.590 --> 00:03:19.610
time.

00:03:19.610 --> 00:03:24.459
People who see this beast in action get given
Class F Amnestics, and they’ve spared no

00:03:24.459 --> 00:03:30.340
expense in suppressing anything about this
coaster to end all coasters in the media.

00:03:30.340 --> 00:03:34.459
But trust us, getting a ride on this thing
is totally more than worth getting on the

00:03:34.459 --> 00:03:36.860
SCP Foundation’s bad side.

00:03:36.860 --> 00:03:37.900
That’s right.

00:03:37.900 --> 00:03:44.319
This killer coaster has a max height of 37.2
meters and a max speed of almost ninety kilometers

00:03:44.319 --> 00:03:45.319
per hour.

00:03:45.319 --> 00:03:48.450
You can’t drive that fast anywhere but the
Autobahn over in Germany!

00:03:48.450 --> 00:03:53.319
Sure, it may technically be “unfinished”,
but this bad boy still has a physical track

00:03:53.319 --> 00:03:55.810
length of 798.8 meters.

00:03:55.810 --> 00:03:59.300
You’re probably wondering why we said “physical”
there, right?

00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:04.680
That’s because, when it comes to SCP-2183,
the real ride starts when the track comes

00:04:04.680 --> 00:04:06.209
to an end, baby!

00:04:06.209 --> 00:04:09.989
When the ride starts a-rollin’, it blasts
down the normal tracks like a bullet, but

00:04:09.989 --> 00:04:13.489
when the track ends and the carts fire off,
they don’t fall.

00:04:13.489 --> 00:04:14.569
No way.

00:04:14.569 --> 00:04:19.419
The carts keep speeding, mid-air, continuing
on the intended track from the rollercoaster’s

00:04:19.419 --> 00:04:21.620
initial badass blueprints.

00:04:21.620 --> 00:04:26.939
But that doesn’t mean this ride does everything
by the book; SCP-2183 is a ride that knows

00:04:26.939 --> 00:04:28.120
how to party.

00:04:28.120 --> 00:04:32.559
There’s never any predicting the exact ride
length, cause every time the carts fire off

00:04:32.559 --> 00:04:37.939
the uncompleted section of track, they take
a totally different path back to the start.

00:04:37.939 --> 00:04:45.039
That makes SCP-2183 officially the most unpredictable
rollercoaster in the entire world!

00:04:45.039 --> 00:04:50.120
The shortest recorded length of the non-physical
section of the track is 1,080 meters, that’s

00:04:50.120 --> 00:04:52.130
almost double the length of the physical track.

00:04:52.130 --> 00:04:58.740
And the maximum length of the non-physical
portion of the track has been 5,460 meters,

00:04:58.740 --> 00:05:03.900
which is over twice the length of the Nagashima
Spa Land’s Steel Dragon 2000, the longest

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:05.610
rollercoaster in the world.

00:05:05.610 --> 00:05:09.020
But we know what you adrenaline junkies are
thinking: It ain’t just the length that

00:05:09.020 --> 00:05:12.249
gets a major buff, it’s also the height
and speed.

00:05:12.249 --> 00:05:16.800
Top recorded heights on the mid-air tracks
have been up to 100 meters, making it the

00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:19.710
fifth tallest rollercoaster in the world.

00:05:19.710 --> 00:05:25.069
And speeds have reached a face-melting 180
kilometers an hour, making it the fourth-fastest

00:05:25.069 --> 00:05:26.839
rollercoaster in the world.

00:05:26.839 --> 00:05:30.550
But maybe, like Shania Twain, that don’t
impress you much.

00:05:30.550 --> 00:05:33.389
We get it, you’re probably thinking, “Fifth
tallest?

00:05:33.389 --> 00:05:34.419
Fourth fastest?

00:05:34.419 --> 00:05:37.689
I thought you said this coaster was truly
hardcore, SCP Explained!”

00:05:37.689 --> 00:05:42.969
But like a good coaster, that’s just because
we haven’t hit you with the big twist yet.

00:05:42.969 --> 00:05:48.479
That twist being: Everything we just told
you only applies to when the carts are empty.

00:05:48.479 --> 00:05:53.120
When someone is actually on this absolute
monster of a rollercoaster, it starts to do

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:55.530
things you wouldn’t believe.

00:05:55.530 --> 00:06:00.249
For you to really understand just how off
the rails this crazy train can go, we’ve

00:06:00.249 --> 00:06:06.219
gotta tell you about D-93730, also known as
The Rider.

00:06:06.219 --> 00:06:10.349
When the Rider woke up that morning, neither
he nor the Foundation researchers handling

00:06:10.349 --> 00:06:13.229
him knew he was going to become a legend.

00:06:13.229 --> 00:06:17.550
As far as D-Classes go, this guy was actually
pretty lucky - seeing that he’d been convicted

00:06:17.550 --> 00:06:22.629
of one of the less severe crimes that constitute
D-Class duty, he was actually part of a release

00:06:22.629 --> 00:06:28.419
program, allowing him to eventually exit the
Foundation alive and return to normal life

00:06:28.419 --> 00:06:31.669
after he’d been involved in a certain number
of studies.

00:06:31.669 --> 00:06:33.500
It seemed like a pretty fair trade.

00:06:33.500 --> 00:06:37.060
However, this was a real “pearls before
swine” situation.

00:06:37.060 --> 00:06:43.100
Any true Coaster Head would relish the opportunity
to take a joyride on SCP-2183; it’d be the

00:06:43.100 --> 00:06:45.539
greatest honor of their lives.

00:06:45.539 --> 00:06:51.159
But for The Rider, all it was was a source
of sweaty palms and an increased heart rate.

00:06:51.159 --> 00:06:53.240
Talk about weaksauce, am I right?

00:06:53.240 --> 00:06:58.720
He had no idea he was in for the ride of his
life, in what would be both the first and

00:06:58.720 --> 00:07:03.219
last human test of SCP-2183.

00:07:03.219 --> 00:07:07.531
They sat him down on one of the carts, strapped
and buckled him in with the safety bar, and

00:07:07.531 --> 00:07:09.499
got that baby rolling.

00:07:09.499 --> 00:07:13.689
When the ride began, the carts took the normal
path down the physical portion of the track,

00:07:13.689 --> 00:07:18.360
but as expected, things got crazy when the
carts hit the anomalous portion.

00:07:18.360 --> 00:07:23.490
Though nobody expected just how crazy this
ride would get, least of all our lucky little

00:07:23.490 --> 00:07:25.369
Rider himself.

00:07:25.369 --> 00:07:28.860
If he could still talk, I’m sure he would
have changed his tune by now.

00:07:28.860 --> 00:07:32.449
The Rider’s cart detached from the rest
during the mid-air portion and took a sharp

00:07:32.449 --> 00:07:36.759
right, going off on its own adventure around
the rest of the abandoned park.

00:07:36.759 --> 00:07:40.659
Everybody knew this was going to be something
special, cause even the Foundation squares

00:07:40.659 --> 00:07:42.949
had never seen a cart act like this before.

00:07:42.949 --> 00:07:47.330
It looped around the whole place several times,
before whizzing through the park like a cruise

00:07:47.330 --> 00:07:51.860
missile, weaving between rides, stalls, and
concession stands with ease.

00:07:51.860 --> 00:07:54.259
It was traveling “blink and you’ll miss
it” fast.

00:07:54.259 --> 00:07:59.430
This thing wasn’t just white-knuckle intense,
it was broken-knuckle intense.

00:07:59.430 --> 00:08:03.400
The rest of the carts returned to the starting
point again and came to a stop, but the Rider

00:08:03.400 --> 00:08:04.949
wasn’t getting off that easy.

00:08:04.949 --> 00:08:10.659
There’s a reason we call SCP-2183 the most
intense rollercoaster in this crazy world

00:08:10.659 --> 00:08:11.659
of ours.

00:08:11.659 --> 00:08:16.090
The cart containing the Rider went AWOL, heading
north out of the park at high speeds, putting

00:08:16.090 --> 00:08:19.059
it on a disastrous collision course with a
nearby town.

00:08:19.059 --> 00:08:22.419
Well, disastrous if you work for the SCP Foundation.

00:08:22.419 --> 00:08:24.050
Totally awesome for the rest of us.

00:08:24.050 --> 00:08:28.839
The thing about a ride on SCP-2183 is that
you really get your money’s worth.

00:08:28.839 --> 00:08:33.289
When people nickname this thing, “The Ride
Never Ends”, they don’t do that just for

00:08:33.289 --> 00:08:34.289
fun.

00:08:34.289 --> 00:08:36.889
This ride literally never ends.

00:08:36.889 --> 00:08:40.529
Over the first few weeks of the Rider’s
ride, the Foundation just tried to suppress

00:08:40.529 --> 00:08:42.699
news of sightings from spreading.

00:08:42.699 --> 00:08:46.730
Multiple people around the nearest Idaho towns
reported seeing a flying rollercoaster cart

00:08:46.730 --> 00:08:48.389
zipping around in the sky.

00:08:48.389 --> 00:08:52.389
Thankfully for the killjoys of the world,
that kind of thing is easily written off as

00:08:52.389 --> 00:08:53.850
a trick of the mind.

00:08:53.850 --> 00:08:57.620
But that didn’t stop the Rider’s epic
thrill-ride from tearing it up all across

00:08:57.620 --> 00:08:58.839
Idaho.

00:08:58.839 --> 00:09:03.370
Over the next few months, this party train
really hit the road - metaphorically speaking,

00:09:03.370 --> 00:09:09.790
of course, this cart consistently remained
120-150 meters above the ground and kept traveling

00:09:09.790 --> 00:09:14.730
at consistent speeds of over 200 kilometers
an hour.

00:09:14.730 --> 00:09:18.860
That makes it roughly tied for the second-fastest
rollercoaster in the world!

00:09:18.860 --> 00:09:23.070
The people lucky enough to spot this bad boy
in action reported that they heard a panicked,

00:09:23.070 --> 00:09:25.610
terrified screaming coming from inside the
cart as it passed.

00:09:25.610 --> 00:09:29.500
That’s how you know that the Rider was having
a helluva time in there!

00:09:29.500 --> 00:09:33.420
Real shame that anyone who spotted it got
a big ol’ dose of Class-A amnestics from

00:09:33.420 --> 00:09:34.980
the killjoy brigade.

00:09:34.980 --> 00:09:39.290
Speaking of those squares, the SCP Foundation
tried multiple times to stop the ride and

00:09:39.290 --> 00:09:42.750
“save” the Rider from this awesome experience.

00:09:42.750 --> 00:09:47.510
They sent in helicopters and lowered ladders
down to him, but the Rider, perhaps finally

00:09:47.510 --> 00:09:52.830
appreciating what a gift he was given here,
kept his arms fastened to his sides, his face

00:09:52.830 --> 00:09:55.230
forced into a permanent grimace.

00:09:55.230 --> 00:10:00.500
Nobody knew how he could still be alive, despite
having no food or water in all this time.

00:10:00.500 --> 00:10:04.879
We can only guess it’s because SCP-2183
is just that awesome.

00:10:04.879 --> 00:10:08.800
Any time these Foundation dweebs tried to
get near the cart, it immediately undertook

00:10:08.800 --> 00:10:12.000
evasive maneuvers and got the hell out of
there.

00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:14.500
Nobody could bring this ultimate ride to an
end!

00:10:14.500 --> 00:10:19.519
In the end, the SCP Foundation proved they
could take being anti-fun to straight-up military

00:10:19.519 --> 00:10:20.519
proportions.

00:10:20.519 --> 00:10:26.759
They approved firing a missile at this piece
of coaster dream-tech, hoping to finally bring

00:10:26.759 --> 00:10:28.910
its awesomeness to an end.

00:10:28.910 --> 00:10:33.500
After making a valiant effort to avoid them,
the missile eventually struck the cart.

00:10:33.500 --> 00:10:38.529
They thought the Rider inside was dead, but
the cart kept flying for another four years

00:10:38.529 --> 00:10:43.940
before finally crashing 34 kilometers from
the rest of the ride, relatively unscathed,

00:10:43.940 --> 00:10:47.269
probably after crashing into one of those
beefy Idaho pigeons.

00:10:47.269 --> 00:10:51.950
And as the Foundation would soon find out,
The Rider was still around too, he just wasn’t

00:10:51.950 --> 00:10:53.250
in the cart anymore.

00:10:53.250 --> 00:11:00.100
Nope, he was suspended in the air in a seated
position 124 meters above the crashed carts.

00:11:00.100 --> 00:11:04.980
We call him the Rider cause he’s still riding
to this very day, and if anyone comes within

00:11:04.980 --> 00:11:10.149
a 50-meter radius of him in any direction,
he’ll just fly away until he’s alone again.

00:11:10.149 --> 00:11:13.800
We don’t know about you, but we think the
Rider’s whole permanent flying situation

00:11:13.800 --> 00:11:19.180
isn’t a horrific purgatory of eternal torment
if he is alive under his comatose state - It’s

00:11:19.180 --> 00:11:20.760
actually the ultimate ride.

00:11:20.760 --> 00:11:24.139
And really, what more could you want out of
life, right?

00:11:24.139 --> 00:11:28.550
Sometimes, people working on the site see
him sitting in the cars, often only for split

00:11:28.550 --> 00:11:29.550
seconds.

00:11:29.550 --> 00:11:31.379
He’s one with the coaster now.

00:11:31.379 --> 00:11:32.600
Total Nirvana.

00:11:32.600 --> 00:11:35.699
Like we said before, kids: The Ride Never
Ends.

00:11:35.699 --> 00:11:43.910
Now go check out “A Sea Snail's Fantasy
SCP-1867 - A Gentleman” and “SCP-5094

00:11:43.910 --> 00:11:49.820
- Miss J's Whiz Kidz Schoolhouse” for more
interesting safe-class SCPs!

